          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:852a342fc19574bf78f894917cfa8cf21ede45b1b8690bf897934d7844be34e0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/page-reader.ts#L155-L185",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:07f7581d7dd015cf1a56ae2f019bc083c6c75fa7e6c31f025123d5e1990c3c4e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f5cf3f8aabf458794fcfaf30f1f553b",
      "statement": "The content-script entrypoint registers a chrome.runtime.onMessage listener whose callback builds a ContentEnvironment from the live page and delegates all extraction/action requests to the shared handleContentRequest (and batch requests to executeBatch), performing no extraction logic itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://clients/extensions/chrome/src/content-script-entry.ts#L346-L418",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d9ce259ebef529cf8a2954f0deaca225814c169dcb77b920c4e6582569cdf2f7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d1b317d57b7e430aa284c51139803916",
      "statement": "To make re-injection safe (ADR 0043), the content script stores its onMessage callback on globalThis.__brijioOnMessageListener and removes any previous injection's listener before adding its own, keeping at most one active listener per page whose pageContextVersion matches the current module scope.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://clients/extensions/chrome/src/content-script-entry.ts#L408-L418",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:34be1433650835acdd37f5c11d87187e41ca52c4200ed024c15c832428bea6bc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0043-idempotent-content-script-injection.md#L40-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:96eb210f1a53fc848f688d19963a8b37b8f8a2062e2914d371f36f01ce9f0efb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5ec7d870d69e44d6b8e9d59ad6a3c7a9",
      "statement": "The background adapter calls scripting.executeScript with content.js before every tabs.sendMessage (for both reads and actions) to ensure the latest content-script code is loaded, relying on the content script's listener replacement to avoid duplicate listeners.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0043-idempotent-content-script-injection.md#L28-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4111fb34abaa916f46be92ca1308a1b0e26a2f0c44c445de7c99cb41ea8b3079:"
